  "recommended_statement": "For every finite ordinary tree T, with x(T) the first strict descent of its zero-extended independence counts and alpha(T) its independence number, and every natural p satisfying x(T)+2 <= p and 3p < 2alpha(T)+1, fix F={original leaves v: Delta_p(T-v)<0}. Let w_F(B) count v in F intersect B for which N_T(s_v) intersects B\\{v}. Between independent (p+1)-sets B and p-sets D, join all w_F(B) upper clones to all w_F(D) lower clones exactly when D=B\\{q} for some q in B, or D=(B\\(N_T(s) intersect B)) union {s} for s not in B with |N_T(s) intersect B|=2. The resulting graph has a matching saturating every upper clone.",
